WEBVTT

00:42.940 --> 00:46.070
Look out! Bandit, one, high! Break!

00:54.520 --> 00:57.920
I'm hit! I'm losing control! Bailing out!

01:12.270 --> 01:14.390
Watch out! That's the Teacher!

01:17.170 --> 01:19.400
He's on my tail! Oh, no!

01:34.720 --> 01:36.350
I'm gonna kill him!

05:28.860 --> 05:29.910
Hi.

05:31.130 --> 05:32.350
Who are you?

05:32.490 --> 05:34.930
I'm Sasakura, the chief mechanic.

05:35.030 --> 05:37.760
I'm Yuichi Kannami. Nice to meet you.

05:40.740 --> 05:43.600
Never seen a female mechanic before?

05:43.710 --> 05:46.830
It's just I feel I've met you
somewhere before.

05:47.480 --> 05:49.270
That's good to hear.

05:52.510 --> 05:55.000
That's the plane you'll be flying.

05:57.850 --> 05:59.380
I can't stick with this one?

05:59.520 --> 06:02.350
A company rep is going to take that back.

06:02.490 --> 06:05.620
They're the same model,
so can't I keep mine?

06:05.730 --> 06:07.820
You'll understand once you fly it.

06:07.930 --> 06:10.630
Besides, that's the boss' order.

06:10.730 --> 06:12.670
Where's the plane's last pilot?

06:12.770 --> 06:14.200
Why do you ask?

06:14.340 --> 06:17.000
Isn't he here to hand over the plane?

06:18.170 --> 06:20.870
You'll have to ask the boss about that.

07:18.370 --> 07:19.530
Enter.

07:31.680 --> 07:34.710
Yuichi Kannami, I've been assigned here.

07:34.850 --> 07:39.480
I'm Suito Kusanagi.
I was expecting you later in the afternoon.

07:42.290 --> 07:44.850
"The glare of the sun was unbearable."

07:46.190 --> 07:50.390
Been reading Camus? You'll be in room 204.

07:50.530 --> 07:52.830
Your roommate's name is Tokino.

07:52.930 --> 07:55.270
You two will go up tomorrow afternoon.

07:55.400 --> 07:56.700
May I...

07:57.610 --> 07:58.770
Sorry.

08:00.780 --> 08:02.110
Excuse me.

10:37.630 --> 10:40.100
I'm Kannami, I was assigned here today.

10:40.200 --> 10:45.370
My name's Yudagawa.
That over there is Uroyuki Shinoda.

10:47.680 --> 10:49.800
How many pilots do you have here?

10:49.910 --> 10:52.880
These days there are three of us, I guess.

10:53.010 --> 10:54.950
That's including you and him?

10:55.050 --> 10:57.880
Starting today, there're four. Including you.

10:58.020 --> 11:00.610
- Just four?
- Yep, just four.

11:00.720 --> 11:04.710
Five, if you include
our enchanting Miss Kusanagi.

11:04.860 --> 11:06.380
She flies, too?

11:08.030 --> 11:09.890
Was he out all night again?

11:20.440 --> 11:21.910
Who are you?

11:22.040 --> 11:25.170
Kannami. I was assigned here today.

11:25.280 --> 11:27.340
Oh, so it's you.

11:31.750 --> 11:33.720
I'm Tokino, your roomie.

11:33.850 --> 11:36.220
I know. I've already been to our room.

11:36.360 --> 11:38.920
I suppose you know
we're going up tomorrow?

11:39.060 --> 11:40.530
Yeah, I know.

11:41.400 --> 11:43.160
Hey, partner.

12:07.420 --> 12:10.550
You don't mean this is your first time,
do you?

12:11.230 --> 12:12.780
The mission? Or this bird?

12:12.930 --> 12:14.050
Bird.

12:14.830 --> 12:17.460
I've been flying Mark B's since I was born.

12:17.600 --> 12:18.690
Yes!

12:53.500 --> 12:57.700
- You tested me?
- Now I see my buddy isn't a chicken.

13:31.270 --> 13:33.570
I don't see anything unusual.

13:34.140 --> 13:37.200
- Let's get home.
- Roger.

13:38.850 --> 13:42.580
Look out! Three bandits!
Same height, 10 o'clock!

15:18.850 --> 15:21.680
- Are you all right?
- No damage.

15:22.420 --> 15:25.540
- How many did you kill?
- Doppel.

16:36.390 --> 16:38.760
- Welcome home, boys.
- Good to be back.

16:44.600 --> 16:46.690
- Losses on our side?
- Zero.

16:47.600 --> 16:51.700
- And Lautern's plant?
- Still inoperative. No sign of activity.

16:52.740 --> 16:55.730
- I see. Well done.
- I'll be going, then.

16:58.380 --> 17:01.040
Would you mind if I asked a question?

17:03.120 --> 17:06.350
It's about the pilot
who had my plane before me.

17:10.820 --> 17:14.450
Jinroh Kurita.
He was transferred here seven months ago.

17:15.300 --> 17:18.860
He had flown 63 sorties.
He was quite a pilot.

17:19.770 --> 17:21.890
Where did he go?

17:22.000 --> 17:24.130
I can't answer that.

17:24.270 --> 17:27.760
- Why was he transferred?
- That, either.

17:27.910 --> 17:29.270
Did he die?

17:29.410 --> 17:32.810
Even if he had,
it wouldn't affect your situation.

17:32.950 --> 17:34.880
To be or not to be.

17:34.980 --> 17:37.750
Those are the only states a human exists in.

17:37.850 --> 17:42.410
Usually a pilot gets to meet
his plane's previous pilot.

17:42.520 --> 17:46.220
Assuming, of course, that he is alive.

17:46.330 --> 17:51.060
That plane is still new.
I decided that it wasn't necessary.

17:51.170 --> 17:52.560
Any problem with it?

17:52.670 --> 17:54.930
No, ma'am, she handled like a champ.

17:55.040 --> 17:56.500
Anything else?

17:57.270 --> 17:59.170
Are you a Kildren?

18:10.820 --> 18:14.450
- Was there anything else?
- I see that you're a smoker.

18:16.160 --> 18:19.350
I don't trust superior officers
who don't smoke.

18:21.200 --> 18:23.030
What's that based on?

18:23.160 --> 18:26.460
That's just been my experience to date.

18:26.570 --> 18:30.370
Experience, huh? Will that be all?

18:30.500 --> 18:32.170
Excuse me, ma'am.

18:55.360 --> 18:58.460
How'd you manage to get two kills that fast?

18:59.870 --> 19:03.100
- Is that flattery?
- I'm lousy at that.

19:03.200 --> 19:05.540
It's just that they were rookies.

19:05.670 --> 19:07.940
- Is that modesty?
- Yep.

19:08.040 --> 19:12.640
- Where were you last stationed?
- Beats me. I can't remember anymore.

19:15.550 --> 19:18.020
- Want to go out tonight?
- Where to?

19:18.150 --> 19:20.350
It seems like it's up to me

19:23.390 --> 19:25.620
to show the new guys around.

19:45.410 --> 19:46.740
What is this place?

19:46.880 --> 19:49.140
The meat pies here are great.

19:50.680 --> 19:52.550
I bet you're starving.

20:32.360 --> 20:33.920
At the end of the engagement,

20:34.060 --> 20:37.660
three of Lautern's twin engine
fighter aircraft, Rainbows, were downed,

20:37.760 --> 20:41.500
and it is reported that two pilots were killed
and another was severely wounded.

20:41.600 --> 20:44.800
On the evening of October 5th,
the situation on the northern front in Europe

20:44.910 --> 20:46.670
has apparently turned more favorable

20:46.770 --> 20:49.800
for one of the two
conflicting warfare companies...

20:52.410 --> 20:57.750
Lately things have gone well for us,
but one day Lautern might get us back.

20:57.880 --> 21:01.320
That was you on the news, right?
Congratulations.

21:04.190 --> 21:07.350
A beer for me,
a meat pie for my friend and a...

21:07.460 --> 21:11.330
A coffee. Why's this place special?

21:11.430 --> 21:15.530
This is point of interest number one.
These things have an order.

21:29.080 --> 21:32.680
I was thinking about telling him
about his predecessor.

21:40.060 --> 21:43.590
- Mama gave me the evil eye.
- "Mama"?

21:45.230 --> 21:49.690
She takes care of our planes, right?
So we call her Mama.

21:51.100 --> 21:53.540
And here comes
point of interest number two!

21:57.480 --> 22:01.240
- Hi, Naofumi!
- Hi!

22:05.420 --> 22:08.980
This is Yuichi Kannami.
He just started with us.

22:09.120 --> 22:11.280
Hi, I'm Kusumi. Nice to meet you.

22:14.290 --> 22:15.660
I'm Fooco.

22:20.600 --> 22:21.930
Hello...

22:33.480 --> 22:35.810
- What did you think?
- About what?

22:35.950 --> 22:37.180
The meat pie.

22:37.320 --> 22:41.190
It was good. It was like
I'd tasted one somewhere before.

23:19.460 --> 23:21.590
So don't worry about it.

23:37.840 --> 23:42.180
- I guess you've been here before, too?
- Maybe I have.

23:42.320 --> 23:45.840
- Bye, Yuichi.
- See you later!

23:45.990 --> 23:47.480
Where's Suito?

23:48.660 --> 23:51.450
How's that scary little lady
doing these days?

23:56.230 --> 23:57.320
Let's go.

23:57.430 --> 23:59.560
- Nice to meet you, boy!
- Nice to meet you, boy!

24:26.460 --> 24:28.220
That smells good.

24:28.360 --> 24:33.560
If you've come here,
I suppose that means that Jinroh is dead.

24:33.700 --> 24:37.930
I don't know.
I don't really know who this Jinroh guy is.

24:39.610 --> 24:43.800
- Want something to drink?
- Coffee would be good, if there's any.

24:45.710 --> 24:49.580
What kind of person was this Jinroh guy?

24:50.850 --> 24:52.340
He was sweet.

24:52.450 --> 24:56.180
His face was innocent like yours
and he had a soft laugh.

24:57.120 --> 25:00.680
But it was like
he was weighed down by something.

25:01.360 --> 25:06.260
That used to make me feel uneasy.
I asked him about it once.

25:07.100 --> 25:10.500
I said, "Where do you keep
misplacing your heart?"

25:12.210 --> 25:15.830
- What did he say?
- He didn't answer.

25:15.940 --> 25:19.240
But I thought maybe he'd left it in the sky.

25:19.380 --> 25:22.910
I thought that would have been
the best for him.

25:24.920 --> 25:27.280
How long have you been here, lady?

25:27.420 --> 25:30.250
"Lady"? Do you mean me?

25:31.260 --> 25:35.700
- That's hilarious.
- It's just you and I here.

25:35.800 --> 25:38.920
Listen to you, you talk like a kid.

25:40.730 --> 25:42.730
That's because I am a kid.

25:48.440 --> 25:50.930
Tell me, do you like flying?

25:51.080 --> 25:54.270
- Sure, I love it.
- Good for you.

25:58.590 --> 26:00.880
- Will you come again?
- Sure.

26:04.420 --> 26:06.320
I'll hold you to that.

26:51.940 --> 26:55.140
Welcome home. So, how did she fly?

26:56.440 --> 27:00.970
She fits like a glove.
It was like the plane was a part of me.

27:03.620 --> 27:07.280
You better believe it.
I don't overlook anything, boy.

27:08.590 --> 27:12.220
The pilot who flew her before me
was named Jinroh, right?

27:12.330 --> 27:13.880
How did he die?

27:15.460 --> 27:19.330
The plane is fine,
so that means that he wasn't shot down.

27:24.870 --> 27:27.170
Go on inside and get some sleep.

29:32.300 --> 29:35.060
- What's wrong?
- I think I'm leaking oil.

29:36.870 --> 29:38.060
What happened?

29:38.200 --> 29:41.070
- Says he has an oil leak.
- Where's Tokino?

29:41.740 --> 29:44.010
I think he'll be back in a minute.

29:47.610 --> 29:50.280
Pinpoint the cause and file a report.

30:26.090 --> 30:28.990
Who are you? I haven't seen you before.

30:29.120 --> 30:31.450
Kannami. I'm a pilot here.

30:31.590 --> 30:34.720
- What's your first name?
- Yuichi.

30:35.600 --> 30:37.430
I'm Mizuki Kusanagi.

30:38.300 --> 30:39.420
What?

30:41.200 --> 30:45.140
I'm Suito Kusanagi's little sister.
I hope we can be friends.

30:45.270 --> 30:48.300
- Sure, me, too.
- What do you mean by that?

30:49.910 --> 30:51.240
You said it first.

30:51.340 --> 30:56.110
What I meant was,
"Let's be friends and talk."

30:56.250 --> 30:58.270
That's what I meant, too.

30:58.420 --> 31:00.750
- Want a drink?
- Sure.

31:00.850 --> 31:02.750
Why did you come here?

31:03.960 --> 31:06.930
My school is on break. So I came to visit.

31:07.660 --> 31:11.120
My sister said I couldn't. But I came anyway.

31:11.260 --> 31:16.130
That's why I was exploring by myself,
so I wouldn't disturb her.

31:17.970 --> 31:21.130
- Want to do something fun?
- Like what?

31:22.680 --> 31:25.110
What do you usually do for fun?

31:25.210 --> 31:29.080
Nothing in particular.
Nothing to brag about.

31:29.180 --> 31:32.170
- Are there any games here?
- Nope.

31:32.320 --> 31:34.680
- Even though you're kids?
- Right.

31:43.630 --> 31:46.860
- Are you a Kildren, Yuichi?
- That's right.

31:47.000 --> 31:49.870
You guys can't become adults, right?

31:50.000 --> 31:52.770
- Right.
- Why can't you become adults?

31:54.370 --> 31:57.610
It's not that we can't, it's that we don't.

31:57.710 --> 32:00.370
Do you want to become an adult?

32:02.480 --> 32:03.970
I'm not sure.

32:05.050 --> 32:06.680
See what I mean?

32:58.070 --> 32:59.560
Oh, wow!

32:59.710 --> 33:01.940
Watch out! It'll hurt your eyes.

33:02.080 --> 33:03.240
That's not fair!

33:03.380 --> 33:06.570
Sorry, could I borrow
a pair of welding goggles?

33:07.210 --> 33:09.550
She wants to watch the sparks.

33:14.120 --> 33:15.280
- Niki.
- Aye.

33:19.760 --> 33:23.960
Thanks. Wow, I can't see a thing in these!

33:25.300 --> 33:26.270
Boo!

33:28.430 --> 33:32.340
It's dangerous, so don't get too close.
Got it?

33:32.470 --> 33:34.000
Yes, ma'am!

33:41.550 --> 33:44.740
- Good work out there.
- What kept you?

33:44.850 --> 33:49.150
I was airborne
so I figured I'd do a little recon.

34:04.370 --> 34:06.600
That girl isn't her little sister.

34:09.810 --> 34:11.110
What are you saying?

34:11.210 --> 34:13.200
That she's her daughter.

34:20.490 --> 34:21.610
I'm back, ma'am.

34:21.720 --> 34:24.490
- Give me your report later.
- Yes, ma'am.

34:24.590 --> 34:26.520
- Sorry.
- That's okay.

34:33.730 --> 34:37.170
When I look at that girl,
I hate myself sometimes.

34:41.910 --> 34:43.170
Why's that?

34:43.280 --> 34:46.510
She's going to catch up
with me before too long.

34:47.080 --> 34:48.810
What am I going to do then?

34:52.450 --> 34:55.850
I have a favor to ask.
A tour group is coming.

34:55.960 --> 34:59.860
- Could you keep them company?
- You think I can do it?

34:59.960 --> 35:03.690
- I have to take her home.
- Understood.

35:09.770 --> 35:11.200
Time to go.

35:41.930 --> 35:44.370
I hear we're getting some tourists.

35:44.470 --> 35:46.700
We've had some before.

35:46.810 --> 35:49.740
Some are affiliated with our sponsors.

35:49.840 --> 35:53.370
Some want to tell you
they're fans of our company.

35:53.480 --> 35:57.540
- What do you think of stuff like that?
- Stuff like what?

35:57.650 --> 36:02.420
- The whole tour group thing.
- I haven't thought about it.

36:03.190 --> 36:05.710
Trust me, you'll want to kill them.

36:07.630 --> 36:10.290
That lady would love to open fire on them.

36:10.430 --> 36:13.660
- What lady?
- The one upstairs.

36:13.800 --> 36:15.960
- You mean Kusanagi?
- Yeah.

36:16.100 --> 36:19.560
- Why do you say that?
- She always has a gun on her.

36:30.280 --> 36:36.950
SECURITY TREATY TO BE SIGNED?

36:41.890 --> 36:45.130
Has anybody told you what
happened to Jinroh Kurita?

36:45.230 --> 36:46.700
Told me what?

36:46.830 --> 36:50.100
- That she shot him.
- Why?

36:55.340 --> 36:57.430
Well, well. Look who's here.

37:06.690 --> 37:08.880
This is our hangar.

37:09.020 --> 37:11.890
Does anyone want me to take their picture?

37:21.370 --> 37:24.800
- Hello, how are you?
- Grand, thank you.

37:24.900 --> 37:28.530
My whole family's big fan of yours.
We're always cheering for your team.

37:28.670 --> 37:29.870
Thank you very much.

37:30.010 --> 37:33.040
- Is that your plane?
- Yes, it is.

37:33.180 --> 37:36.010
- What is it like?
- What's what like?

37:36.120 --> 37:41.050
- I mean, how does it feel to fly?
- Well, I don't know what to say.

37:41.190 --> 37:43.660
What about when you shoot down
an enemy plane?

37:43.760 --> 37:45.050
I feel like a winner.

37:45.190 --> 37:49.360
- Don't you put a kill mark on your plane?
- Some do, but I don't.

37:49.460 --> 37:50.720
It's just like a game.

37:50.860 --> 37:55.270
I know, war is always horrible.
You're fighting for a peaceful world.

37:55.400 --> 37:58.340
We really appreciate
what you're doing for us.

37:58.440 --> 37:59.870
It's my job.

38:23.630 --> 38:25.190
He's going down.

39:06.210 --> 39:07.900
Is it one of ours?

39:08.010 --> 39:12.570
It's the same model as ours,
but it drifted in from the adjacent theater.

39:18.720 --> 39:22.180
God, help him.

39:23.690 --> 39:25.160
Poor boy.

39:33.200 --> 39:34.860
Enough is enough!

39:36.400 --> 39:38.130
He's not a poor boy!

39:39.670 --> 39:44.870
Don't pity him!
How dare you insult him with your pity!

39:48.550 --> 39:49.880
Calm down.

41:41.690 --> 41:45.320
Seven days in jail on bread and water.
You'd be singing.

41:58.810 --> 42:01.800
It is determined by identification of
the downed aircraft

42:01.950 --> 42:05.310
that it is a Rostock Sanka B fighter
from the 502 squadron

42:05.450 --> 42:09.680
stationed at neighboring District 202,
but that the details are not available yet.

42:09.820 --> 42:13.120
Public affairs officials at the company
have declined to answer further questions

42:13.230 --> 42:14.850
concerning this incident.

42:18.830 --> 42:21.320
- You want me to get her?
- Get who?

42:21.470 --> 42:23.460
Well, you know, your...

42:23.570 --> 42:27.700
Oh, her.
No, I'm going back once I'm done eating.

43:19.060 --> 43:21.080
- This is Kannami.
- Where are you?

43:21.230 --> 43:24.890
- At Daniel's.
- I hate to be rude but I can't speak now.

43:25.030 --> 43:27.500
Three Fortune bombers
are heading your way.

43:27.600 --> 43:29.930
- You mean two.
- No, there are three.

43:30.070 --> 43:31.370
- You saw them?
- Yes.

43:31.470 --> 43:34.740
- How long have we got?
- Less than five minutes.

43:34.870 --> 43:38.500
That gives us time,
but you won't be back by then.

43:38.610 --> 43:40.580
- What about my plane?
- I'll fly it.

43:40.710 --> 43:42.540
Take good care of her.

43:45.120 --> 43:46.780
Going back to the base?

43:46.920 --> 43:49.620
Yeah, even though
there'll be no planes to fly.

43:49.760 --> 43:51.120
Be careful.

43:53.290 --> 43:54.920
Careful of what?

44:01.500 --> 44:02.730
Yuichi!

44:07.410 --> 44:10.070
- Yuichi!
- Yuichi!

44:11.640 --> 44:14.880
Is everything okay?
We saw some big planes fly overhead.

44:14.980 --> 44:17.740
- The base is under attack.
- Is Naofumi okay?

44:17.850 --> 44:21.050
- I don't know.
- We'll drive you there.

44:21.150 --> 44:24.280
I can't ditch this here. It's a loaner.

44:24.420 --> 44:27.090
- We'll meet you there, then.
- Sure.

44:51.120 --> 44:55.490
- All our planes airborne?
- Your bird gave us some trouble.

44:55.620 --> 44:57.610
She's up there without a spinner.

44:57.720 --> 45:01.780
And we had no time to fuel her
so she'll soon be out of gas.

45:01.890 --> 45:04.160
- Kusanagi's flying her?
- Yeah.

45:08.170 --> 45:11.860
It's Naofumi! Naofumi!

45:12.540 --> 45:16.840
You ought to get rid of those girls
while you still can.

45:16.980 --> 45:19.970
Kusanagi will start yelling
if she sees them here.

45:20.080 --> 45:21.940
Who will she yell at?

45:22.380 --> 45:25.010
You gave them permission to come here.

45:25.150 --> 45:26.620
Yuichi!

45:26.720 --> 45:30.280
Now we know he's okay, we're going!

45:30.390 --> 45:33.120
Bye-bye, Yuichi!

46:07.790 --> 46:09.730
I don't need your help.

46:17.140 --> 46:20.330
- I wonder what's keeping Tokino.
- He's definitely safe.

46:20.440 --> 46:24.670
- He circled the base a minute ago.
- He must have landed somewhere.

46:28.110 --> 46:30.550
It's me. Get me Theater Command.

46:31.380 --> 46:33.870
Sorry, do you have any cigarettes?

46:47.130 --> 46:49.730
This is Kusanagi.
Put me through to the manager.

46:51.070 --> 46:53.300
I don't care, just put him on the phone!

46:54.910 --> 46:56.770
Yes, miraculously enough.

46:56.910 --> 47:00.780
The damage isn't too bad,
only because they botched the job.

47:01.510 --> 47:03.880
Why did it take you so long to warn us?

47:04.820 --> 47:07.880
That's not much of a reason.
I'm coming there, now.

47:07.990 --> 47:11.980
Yudagawa! Can you man
my desk until I get back?

47:12.590 --> 47:14.720
We might get an emergency call.

47:15.330 --> 47:17.820
Sure, if I can eat and drink up there.

47:17.960 --> 47:19.330
Of course.

47:19.460 --> 47:21.330
Kannami, come with me.

47:31.340 --> 47:32.780
Aren't we going a little fast?

47:32.880 --> 47:35.280
Sorry, I'm in that kind of mood.

47:39.720 --> 47:43.120
- Look, it's Tokino.
- I knew it, he was goofing off.

47:43.960 --> 47:49.160
That stretch of road in front of the diner
is perfect for making emergency landings.

47:49.830 --> 47:52.320
You know, to grab a cup of coffee.

48:32.440 --> 48:35.670
What an honor to be greeted at the door.

48:35.770 --> 48:37.710
It's been a long time.

48:37.840 --> 48:40.640
I guess you're not going to let me in?

48:42.080 --> 48:46.980
No sign here of a major disaster
that kept you from warning us.

48:50.360 --> 48:52.020
He's one of my men.

48:52.120 --> 48:57.320
I thought if I felt drained after this visit,
he could drive me back to the base.

48:58.300 --> 49:01.060
We've heard about you.

49:02.700 --> 49:04.830
The manager is out at the moment.

49:04.940 --> 49:09.270
Well, if you let me take a look,
I'd soon know if he's in or not.

49:09.940 --> 49:12.040
Having come all this way

49:12.140 --> 49:15.270
makes the gravity
of the situation quite clear.

49:15.410 --> 49:18.110
We understand your feelings on this matter.

49:18.250 --> 49:23.380
You've got the wrong idea.
I want to see the man who almost killed us.

49:27.290 --> 49:29.620
I swear, she's so immature.

49:29.760 --> 49:32.390
This is the problem with children.

49:32.500 --> 49:34.470
Oh, no offense meant.

49:34.600 --> 49:36.260
No, you're right.

49:37.340 --> 49:42.360
But do people who might die tomorrow
have any need to grow up?

49:58.520 --> 50:01.050
- Make a right at the fork up ahead.
- What?

50:02.290 --> 50:04.660
I want to make a stop somewhere.

50:48.810 --> 50:50.500
Has anyone called?

50:51.180 --> 50:55.310
I see. Sure, you can go.
Get some rest, thanks.

51:09.090 --> 51:10.960
What is this place?

51:11.060 --> 51:13.030
It's like a guesthouse.

51:15.030 --> 51:19.200
It's for the employees,
so we're expected to use it.

51:19.340 --> 51:22.000
No one ever comes here twice, though.

51:23.440 --> 51:26.240
Oh, so everyone comes here once.

51:26.380 --> 51:27.740
With you.

51:27.880 --> 51:30.970
It's rare for me to come here
alone with someone.

51:31.080 --> 51:32.480
Why's that?

51:33.590 --> 51:35.350
You must be hungry.

51:35.450 --> 51:38.820
There's only frozen food,
but I'll make something.

52:00.210 --> 52:03.880
- I'm amazed that you can eat that.
- Why?

52:03.980 --> 52:08.940
- Because it tastes awful.
- It's made from edible ingredients, right?

52:15.630 --> 52:17.420
You want to go back?

52:20.400 --> 52:22.590
We can spend the night here.

52:41.520 --> 52:44.720
Did that guy, Jinroh
spend the night here, too?

52:46.020 --> 52:47.080
Yes.

52:48.660 --> 52:49.890
Why do you ask?

52:52.030 --> 52:54.260
Yudagawa told me a funny story.

52:56.330 --> 52:58.800
He said that you killed Jinroh.

53:08.110 --> 53:10.080
Are you trying to tell me

53:12.020 --> 53:14.510
that you want me to kill you, too?

53:37.640 --> 53:39.670
Five minutes to bingo fuel.

53:42.080 --> 53:45.680
Let's go home. Turn right to one-six-zero.

53:45.820 --> 53:47.550
Maintain this height.

53:56.360 --> 53:57.660
Look out, bandits.

53:57.760 --> 54:00.230
Two o'clock high, Doppel bombers.

54:04.870 --> 54:06.530
They've got escorts.

54:06.670 --> 54:10.570
- Rainbows?
- One is a prop-forward. Maybe a J-2.

54:11.440 --> 54:14.070
- Are you sure?
- Wanna bet?

54:17.380 --> 54:20.320
I'll check it out. You head home.

54:20.420 --> 54:24.250
By yourself? No way! Come back, Westy!

54:30.130 --> 54:32.100
Westy, come in! Where are you?

54:32.230 --> 54:34.060
It's a J-2.

54:34.530 --> 54:38.020
Black jaguar on the nose! The Teacher!

54:38.640 --> 54:40.040
"Teacher"?

54:41.310 --> 54:43.000
Bug out, Yuichi!

55:08.630 --> 55:12.590
Westy, are you all right? Where are you?

55:12.740 --> 55:15.070
Come in! Answer me!

55:55.210 --> 55:58.410
- Yudagawa said it was the Teacher?
- Yes.

56:06.120 --> 56:07.490
You can go.

56:42.060 --> 56:45.190
NO FAIR WARNING!

56:50.900 --> 56:54.360
We were over the water.
His plane sank like a stone.

56:54.510 --> 56:56.030
You saw it happen?

56:59.680 --> 57:03.370
We haven't had Skylys in our theater before,

57:05.450 --> 57:09.680
so he was probably curious to see
if the pilot was the Teacher.

57:09.790 --> 57:11.310
Who's this "Teacher"?

57:11.420 --> 57:14.980
If you run into him up there,
you don't come back.

57:16.290 --> 57:19.390
They say he's Lautern's ace pilot.

57:20.100 --> 57:25.870
Maybe he was sent here to this theater
because we've been winning too often.

57:26.700 --> 57:28.540
That sounds likely.

57:36.410 --> 57:37.850
The Teacher.

57:42.950 --> 57:47.190
This is just a rumor,
but they say he isn't like us.

57:47.290 --> 57:49.190
They say he's an adult.

57:49.290 --> 57:51.850
Even though he's a fighter pilot?

57:51.960 --> 57:56.260
Yeah. He's an adult. An adult man.

57:58.070 --> 57:59.930
An adult man.

01:01:20.140 --> 01:01:22.770
- Has there been any word?
- No, nothing.

01:01:26.240 --> 01:01:29.150
I told her that we should turn back.

01:01:29.280 --> 01:01:31.910
The weather was bad
and we were low on fuel.

01:01:32.020 --> 01:01:33.810
She agreed then, but...

01:01:33.950 --> 01:01:35.440
What happened?

01:01:36.620 --> 01:01:40.280
She saw a bandit in the distance
and broke away.

01:01:40.430 --> 01:01:42.590
Now that she hasn't come back...

01:01:42.690 --> 01:01:47.130
Lay off the beer. We might have to
go on a search if the weather clears.

01:01:48.400 --> 01:01:49.830
That was the Teacher!

01:01:49.970 --> 01:01:51.530
Did you see the black jaguar?

01:01:51.670 --> 01:01:55.130
If I'd been close enough to see,
I'd have joined her!

01:01:55.670 --> 01:01:58.470
Why is she so obsessed with the Teacher?

01:01:58.580 --> 01:02:01.200
When she comes back, ask her yourself.

01:02:01.350 --> 01:02:03.540
If she comes back, you mean.

01:03:22.090 --> 01:03:23.420
Out of the way!

01:03:26.700 --> 01:03:29.890
- Get a doctor!
- Get me some blankets!

01:03:33.440 --> 01:03:36.100
She made an emergency landing
near my place.

01:03:36.210 --> 01:03:37.440
Thanks.

01:03:38.540 --> 01:03:42.340
I've seen her like this once before.

01:03:45.580 --> 01:03:50.180
Like something had plowed
straight into her, right here.

01:03:52.020 --> 01:03:56.820
A long time ago, she came to our place

01:03:56.930 --> 01:03:58.290
to see a client of mine.

01:04:02.530 --> 01:04:06.300
She made me leave
and didn't come out again for hours.

01:04:25.990 --> 01:04:28.650
That girl is dangerous.

01:04:33.760 --> 01:04:36.290
What are you gawking at? Go outside!

01:04:36.400 --> 01:04:37.630
Yes, ma'am!

01:04:45.810 --> 01:04:47.900
Got any smokes?

01:04:55.750 --> 01:05:00.620
Sorry I caused you trouble.
Tell the men that, too.

01:05:03.190 --> 01:05:04.920
She passed out, that's all.

01:05:05.030 --> 01:05:07.790
Seems like her bones and organs are okay.

01:05:07.930 --> 01:05:11.060
Let her sleep until the doctor gets here.

01:05:11.170 --> 01:05:13.760
A large-scale project is in the works.

01:05:13.870 --> 01:05:16.860
So our squadron might have to move, too.

01:05:17.010 --> 01:05:18.480
Move?

01:05:18.580 --> 01:05:20.810
It'll only be temporary.

01:05:20.910 --> 01:05:25.440
But I think she wanted to settle the score
before we left.

01:05:30.550 --> 01:05:33.890
You and Kusanagi go back
a long way, right?

01:05:34.030 --> 01:05:35.190
What about it?

01:05:35.290 --> 01:05:40.490
That girl, Mizuki.
Do you think that her father could be...

01:05:43.630 --> 01:05:47.470
I'll stay with her until the doctor comes.
Go and get some sleep.

01:07:59.600 --> 01:08:03.870
I swear, no matter where you go,
the people are always the same.

01:08:04.540 --> 01:08:07.910
I hardly ever see someone
who makes me think,

01:08:08.050 --> 01:08:10.740
"I've never seen anybody like this before."

01:08:10.880 --> 01:08:13.350
Aren't twin pilots pretty unusual?

01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:16.210
There's been a few sets before.

01:08:16.320 --> 01:08:20.050
But you never see one of
them come back by himself.

01:08:28.200 --> 01:08:30.170
What are you two doing?

01:08:31.670 --> 01:08:33.830
Those rides are for the kids.

01:08:33.970 --> 01:08:36.100
Well, I happen to be a kid.

01:08:41.980 --> 01:08:44.880
Is a guy named Kannami still at the party?

01:08:45.920 --> 01:08:47.470
I don't think he's there anymore.

01:08:47.590 --> 01:08:51.020
- Is he in his quarters?
- I don't think he's there yet.

01:08:54.190 --> 01:08:57.520
- Let me guess, you're him?
- Could be.

01:08:57.630 --> 01:09:01.030
- Why didn't you say so?
- You didn't ask.

01:09:06.840 --> 01:09:10.500
You know,
you're nothing at all like I imagined.

01:09:10.640 --> 01:09:13.440
I'm Tokino. Am I like what you imagined?

01:09:14.310 --> 01:09:17.610
- I'm Mitsuya. Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

01:09:19.320 --> 01:09:21.680
I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

01:09:33.260 --> 01:09:35.660
Jeez, what's the deal with her?

01:09:53.180 --> 01:09:55.620
That was one impressive specimen, huh?

01:09:55.750 --> 01:09:58.240
- What was?
- That chick last night.

01:09:59.820 --> 01:10:01.950
They say she's their ace.

01:10:02.830 --> 01:10:06.350
Female aces never go along
with what you want them to.

01:10:06.500 --> 01:10:09.020
It's the same with male aces.

01:10:12.240 --> 01:10:14.600
Who gives a damn about male aces!

01:10:14.710 --> 01:10:17.270
Look at you, you're our ace!

01:10:17.370 --> 01:10:20.100
I hear Kusanagi was a good pilot, too.

01:10:21.080 --> 01:10:23.480
When will you make a move?

01:10:23.580 --> 01:10:27.310
Well, you're free to do your own thing,
I guess.

01:10:27.420 --> 01:10:28.680
Do what?

01:10:29.620 --> 01:10:32.180
To do whatever you want, bozo!

01:10:35.730 --> 01:10:38.060
You are about to take part

01:10:38.160 --> 01:10:41.720
in a project of unprecedented
scale this afternoon.

01:10:43.270 --> 01:10:47.800
The target is Lautern's largest
stronghold in the central theater.

01:10:48.840 --> 01:10:53.440
First, your eight fighters
will lift off from this base.

01:10:53.540 --> 01:10:57.240
You'll rendezvous with friendly fighters
from other bases.

01:10:57.350 --> 01:10:59.940
That's 80 fighters all together.

01:11:00.050 --> 01:11:04.320
Plus 30 medium bombers
and 20 heavy bombers at high altitude.

01:11:04.420 --> 01:11:06.050
This is Team B.

01:11:06.190 --> 01:11:11.130
Team A will have 40 fighters
and 50 air-to-ground attack craft.

01:11:11.230 --> 01:11:16.330
They'll strike the two frontline bases
before you arrive.

01:11:17.130 --> 01:11:18.660
Any questions?

01:11:20.640 --> 01:11:23.870
May I ask a question unrelated
to the mission?

01:11:23.970 --> 01:11:25.030
Go ahead.

01:11:25.140 --> 01:11:27.370
Will tonight's party be canceled?

01:11:27.480 --> 01:11:28.950
Another party?

01:11:29.080 --> 01:11:33.310
Every other month,
we hold parties for the local kids.

01:11:33.450 --> 01:11:35.280
That night is tonight.

01:11:35.420 --> 01:11:37.580
My apologies. I didn't know.

01:11:38.360 --> 01:11:41.590
It'll go ahead. This mission is classified.

01:11:41.690 --> 01:11:44.660
Canceling the party would be suspicious.

01:11:46.560 --> 01:11:49.190
Do you have anything to add, Kusanagi?

01:11:50.200 --> 01:11:52.960
We'll encounter the enemy over the sea.

01:11:53.800 --> 01:11:57.760
After their bases are attacked,
we can expect a counter-attack.

01:11:58.880 --> 01:12:03.510
If their fighters are overhead
they can't intercept us with fire.

01:12:03.610 --> 01:12:05.670
They'll try to push us back.

01:12:05.780 --> 01:12:09.650
This is an unusually
long-range strike mission for us.

01:12:10.490 --> 01:12:14.290
Our short-range Sankas
will be refueled midair.

01:12:14.390 --> 01:12:17.260
Keep your drop tanks until the last minute.

01:12:17.360 --> 01:12:18.760
That's all.

01:12:20.960 --> 01:12:23.260
Okay, assemble on
the runway in 20 minutes.

01:14:29.360 --> 01:14:33.300
Rostock, contractor warfare company
for the European Confederation,

01:14:33.430 --> 01:14:37.990
began long-range raids against strategically
vital facilities of its opponent, Lautern,

01:14:38.140 --> 01:14:41.590
and it's expected that more
large-scale engagements will ensue.

01:14:41.710 --> 01:14:45.230
The strength of the attacking force is,
according to the statement by Rostock,

01:14:45.340 --> 01:14:48.240
three squadrons of heavy bombers from
the Strategic Bombardment Wing

01:14:48.350 --> 01:14:52.750
escorted by fighters from eight squadrons
and four tactical squadrons.

01:15:12.570 --> 01:15:16.160
Fighter control to fighters,
six-two-zero-zero to waypoint one.

01:15:17.140 --> 01:15:21.870
Estimated time of contact correction,
ten-zero-zero minus zero-five.

01:15:22.510 --> 01:15:25.680
Repeat, ten-zero-zero minus zero-five.

01:15:26.880 --> 01:15:31.340
Fighter squadrons Able, Baker, Charlie,
stay on your altitude.

01:15:47.910 --> 01:15:50.200
Whales, climb and evacuate.

01:16:08.760 --> 01:16:12.490
Warning, enemy in sight.
Altitude, eighty-zero-zero.

01:16:12.600 --> 01:16:15.190
Fighters contact and engage at will.

01:16:15.330 --> 01:16:17.860
All weapons free! Let's dance!

01:18:35.510 --> 01:18:38.770
Control to everyone. Evacuate battle area.

01:18:38.880 --> 01:18:41.500
Repeat, evacuate battle area.

01:18:44.150 --> 01:18:46.480
Cairn, where are you?

01:18:48.120 --> 01:18:50.780
Altitude thirty-zero-zero, turning left to join.

01:18:51.390 --> 01:18:55.150
Tally-ho. Joining up low, 4 o'clock.

01:18:55.290 --> 01:18:57.920
- Where's Scotty?
- No joy.

01:18:58.800 --> 01:19:01.130
Scotty, come in. This is Cairn.

01:19:01.800 --> 01:19:05.260
I get no answer. Mission complete.

01:19:05.370 --> 01:19:10.030
RTB, everyone.
Repeat, return to base, everyone.

01:19:11.140 --> 01:19:14.110
Rostock's big offensive that started
at 10:00 this morning

01:19:14.210 --> 01:19:17.700
met with unexpectedly fierce
and effective interception from Lautern

01:19:17.850 --> 01:19:22.620
and fell into total confusion,
inflicting heavy casualties to both sides.

01:19:22.720 --> 01:19:24.280
The engagements seem to be halted

01:19:24.390 --> 01:19:28.480
as a recommendation was hastily issued
from the European Confederation.

01:19:28.590 --> 01:19:30.890
We will report the precise figures
of losses and casualties

01:19:31.030 --> 01:19:34.720
of both conflicting companies as soon as
the Conflict Control Committee will...

01:20:02.560 --> 01:20:04.050
- Where are you?
- We're busy here!

01:20:22.880 --> 01:20:25.250
Looks like they lost some, too.

01:20:26.120 --> 01:20:30.450
- Did you see them go down?
- Theirs, or ours?

01:20:40.800 --> 01:20:46.390
The Skyly came up behind Kishinuma
and almost caught him.

01:20:46.500 --> 01:20:50.560
And he did a half roll
and raised the nose like this.

01:20:50.670 --> 01:20:55.870
The Skyly's stall turn let Kumatake
pass as he covered Kishinuma.

01:20:55.980 --> 01:20:59.470
Then he did a snap roll
and closed in on Kumatake.

01:21:00.680 --> 01:21:05.140
He opened fire, point-blank.
He probably got Shinoda the same way.

01:21:06.260 --> 01:21:09.120
The Skyly had a black jaguar on its nose.

01:21:14.460 --> 01:21:17.260
Once this is over,
let's check out the new city.

01:21:32.320 --> 01:21:35.010
Man, doesn't this place have any bars?

01:21:36.650 --> 01:21:38.990
Let's get off at the next stop.

01:22:48.560 --> 01:22:51.530
They sure close early. It's not late at all.

01:22:52.260 --> 01:22:57.500
What a decent and orderly city!
Hey, what's that look like to you?

01:23:08.810 --> 01:23:13.510
- Well, what a coincidence!
- You're going bowling?

01:23:13.620 --> 01:23:16.450
We might be able to get beer there.

01:23:19.390 --> 01:23:23.350
Almost! Go for the spare! Let's roll!

01:23:58.330 --> 01:24:01.090
What the hell was that supposed to be?

01:24:01.200 --> 01:24:02.430
Tokino.

01:24:42.040 --> 01:24:43.840
Your turn, Kannami.

01:25:11.370 --> 01:25:12.890
Don't wait up!

01:25:16.940 --> 01:25:21.540
I'd love to line up those bimbos
and knock them down.

01:25:23.410 --> 01:25:25.750
Want to play another game?

01:25:25.880 --> 01:25:29.580
Let's ask the staff here
about somewhere we can get a drink.

01:25:45.600 --> 01:25:47.570
I can't drink anymore.

01:25:50.770 --> 01:25:52.540
I'll have it, then.

01:26:03.450 --> 01:26:06.890
Why were you so reckless
that day you got shot down?

01:26:08.390 --> 01:26:11.260
Was it the plane's black jaguar marking?

01:26:12.100 --> 01:26:15.090
Years ago, he was one of our employees.

01:26:15.730 --> 01:26:19.070
An employee?
But you talk about him with respect.

01:26:20.400 --> 01:26:22.460
Because he was my superior officer.

01:26:22.610 --> 01:26:27.740
You see, he's unique as a pilot.
He's an ordinary adult.

01:26:28.610 --> 01:26:30.080
An adult man.

01:26:31.610 --> 01:26:33.880
Why did he go over to Lautern?

01:26:34.750 --> 01:26:38.710
Some things happened and he quit Rostock.

01:26:39.360 --> 01:26:42.550
What would change
if you shot down the Teacher?

01:26:43.630 --> 01:26:47.490
Like your destiny or your limits, perhaps?

01:26:49.030 --> 01:26:50.500
I'm not sure.

01:26:51.530 --> 01:26:53.800
But no one can shoot him down.

01:26:53.940 --> 01:26:55.170
Why not?

01:26:57.470 --> 01:27:01.070
Who or what do you think it is
that we're fighting?

01:27:01.180 --> 01:27:03.650
Beats me. I've never thought about it.

01:27:03.780 --> 01:27:05.580
Even though we kill each other?

01:27:05.680 --> 01:27:09.640
It's a job. It's the same as any business.

01:27:10.520 --> 01:27:13.420
The powerful one makes a profit and wins.

01:27:14.720 --> 01:27:18.090
Compared to regular jobs,
we are more inefficient

01:27:18.190 --> 01:27:20.750
like we're playing an archaic game.

01:27:20.860 --> 01:27:26.100
You're right.
That's why we can kill and be killed legally.

01:27:26.800 --> 01:27:28.270
That's an interesting view.

01:27:28.370 --> 01:27:29.800
Interesting?

01:27:31.570 --> 01:27:36.030
War has never been completely
eradicated in history.

01:27:36.180 --> 01:27:40.170
Because its sense of reality
is essential to humans.

01:27:40.820 --> 01:27:45.810
Having wars going on out there somewhere

01:27:45.920 --> 01:27:49.290
sustains the illusion of peace in our society.

01:27:49.890 --> 01:27:52.730
And it has to be real, with no charades.

01:27:53.330 --> 01:27:57.130
Reading about wars in history books
isn't enough.

01:27:57.230 --> 01:27:59.720
That's too much like a fairy tale.

01:28:00.440 --> 01:28:04.700
If people don't get to see
actual deaths on the news,

01:28:04.840 --> 01:28:08.830
if misery isn't displayed,
peace can't be maintained.

01:28:09.550 --> 01:28:12.340
The significance of peace
would be forgotten.

01:28:12.450 --> 01:28:15.080
People need wars to feel alive,

01:28:15.220 --> 01:28:18.480
just like we feel alive
when we fight in the sky.

01:28:20.190 --> 01:28:25.680
And because our war is a game
that is not supposed to ever end,

01:28:25.800 --> 01:28:28.390
some rules are needed.

01:28:28.530 --> 01:28:33.090
For example, there must be an enemy
who cannot be defeated.

01:28:34.040 --> 01:28:36.510
And that's the Teacher?

01:29:06.240 --> 01:29:08.700
Don't you think you've had enough?

01:29:27.720 --> 01:29:29.490
Can I help you?

01:30:07.460 --> 01:30:09.590
Do you want me to kill you?

01:30:13.000 --> 01:30:16.130
Or will you do me a favor and kill me?

01:30:17.340 --> 01:30:21.400
Or else nothing will ever change for us.

01:31:47.230 --> 01:31:49.820
Only two planes came back.

01:31:49.930 --> 01:31:53.230
Those Someakas will make
the fleet a mixed one.

01:31:53.370 --> 01:31:55.530
Their engines are complicated.

01:31:55.640 --> 01:31:59.370
Rokuta, Haga and Niki
can deal with twin engines.

01:32:35.240 --> 01:32:36.970
Hey! Loverboy!

01:32:40.520 --> 01:32:44.480
- Yeah, what?
- What's with that little girl?

01:32:44.620 --> 01:32:46.750
She's Kusanagi's daughter.

01:32:46.860 --> 01:32:50.620
Her daughter? Well then who's the father?

01:32:50.760 --> 01:32:52.890
There're lots of rumors on that subject.

01:33:26.700 --> 01:33:28.600
Who are you?

01:33:28.700 --> 01:33:31.430
I'm a pilot that was assigned here.

01:33:31.530 --> 01:33:33.000
I'm Kannami.

01:33:33.140 --> 01:33:36.200
I'm Aihara.
How many pilots are stationed here?

01:33:36.340 --> 01:33:39.470
There're seven,
if we include you and the boss.

01:34:00.600 --> 01:34:01.790
Are you okay?

01:34:01.900 --> 01:34:06.060
Yeah, there used to be a guy here
who folded his paper like that.

01:34:22.280 --> 01:34:27.520
ALL AGRICULTURAL IMPORTS BANNED

01:36:17.000 --> 01:36:21.300
Chief Sasakura,
how long have you worked with Kusanagi?

01:36:21.400 --> 01:36:24.500
I don't know, I guess about eight years now.

01:36:24.610 --> 01:36:28.040
So you knew her
when she was the ace pilot here.

01:36:28.180 --> 01:36:29.470
Yeah, I guess.

01:36:29.580 --> 01:36:32.210
What do you make of her decline?

01:36:33.550 --> 01:36:35.710
What do you mean by that?

01:36:38.020 --> 01:36:39.890
She is self-destructing.

01:36:40.020 --> 01:36:44.190
It seems like she's carrying out
her duties just fine.

01:36:44.290 --> 01:36:47.820
- She had that child.
- What about it?

01:36:47.930 --> 01:36:50.760
- A child had a child!
- What about it?

01:36:50.900 --> 01:36:52.770
- Don't you get it?
- No, I don't.

01:36:52.900 --> 01:36:56.860
Everybody's like you,
they just turn a blind eye!

01:36:56.970 --> 01:37:00.430
The company's the same!
They must know, too.

01:37:00.580 --> 01:37:02.410
Look here, Kusanagi is...

01:37:06.050 --> 01:37:09.350
Because she was an incredible ace,
she survived.

01:37:09.450 --> 01:37:12.180
She got to live longer than the others.

01:37:12.790 --> 01:37:16.420
Just long enough to see
and think about things more.

01:37:16.560 --> 01:37:20.120
She learned to act on
her own fate and that of others'.

01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:24.630
You mean like how
she killed the man she loved?

01:37:24.770 --> 01:37:26.260
Don't you get it?

01:37:26.370 --> 01:37:27.800
No, I don't!

01:37:49.560 --> 01:37:51.420
I'm leaving now.

01:37:51.530 --> 01:37:53.960
- To Kusumi's?
- Yep.

01:37:54.060 --> 01:37:56.160
Tell Fooco that I said hi.

01:38:08.240 --> 01:38:09.770
So, who is it?

01:38:09.880 --> 01:38:10.940
What do you mean?

01:38:11.050 --> 01:38:14.480
Who is it that you agreed to meet tonight?

01:38:16.490 --> 01:38:18.980
If it's Kusanagi, you'd better forget it.

01:38:20.490 --> 01:38:23.220
No. You're not meeting up
with Mitsuya, are you?

01:38:23.360 --> 01:38:26.820
Please, anybody but her.
You should reconsider.

01:38:26.930 --> 01:38:29.660
What's so dangerous about those two?

01:38:29.770 --> 01:38:33.960
Trust me. Sleep with Kusanagi,

01:38:34.070 --> 01:38:36.970
and she'll blow your brains out.
It's goodbye, Yuichi!

01:38:37.070 --> 01:38:38.400
What about Mitsuya?

01:38:38.540 --> 01:38:41.700
You'd never escape. She's like an ant trap.

01:38:42.510 --> 01:38:44.480
Any more advice for me?

01:38:47.120 --> 01:38:49.640
I'm not about to plead with you,

01:38:49.750 --> 01:38:52.720
but let me give you some heartfelt advice.

01:38:53.960 --> 01:38:56.480
- Watch your back tonight.
- Thanks.

01:39:11.640 --> 01:39:12.900
Come in.

01:39:14.080 --> 01:39:15.910
Do you have a minute?

01:39:20.620 --> 01:39:24.180
If you don't mind coffee,
there's some on the table.

01:39:46.510 --> 01:39:49.770
I'm glad you didn't go out tonight.

01:39:49.910 --> 01:39:51.640
Tokino did.

01:39:51.780 --> 01:39:53.580
To see that adult woman?

01:39:53.680 --> 01:39:54.940
Right.

01:39:55.080 --> 01:39:56.780
Why did you stay in?

01:39:56.920 --> 01:39:59.050
I had a funny feeling.

01:39:59.150 --> 01:40:01.490
That I would stop by for a visit?

01:40:01.620 --> 01:40:03.990
I'm not that full of myself.

01:40:04.130 --> 01:40:08.320
I had a hunch I should stay in.
They're usually right.

01:40:08.460 --> 01:40:12.460
Kannami, how long
have you been stationed at this base?

01:40:13.140 --> 01:40:15.900
I don't know...
Maybe since the end of summer?

01:40:16.010 --> 01:40:18.940
How many flight hours have you logged?

01:40:19.040 --> 01:40:22.140
How many years have you been a pilot?

01:40:22.240 --> 01:40:25.150
Is that what you want to talk about?

01:40:25.250 --> 01:40:28.980
I wanted to ask you some questions
because I trust you.

01:40:29.080 --> 01:40:32.540
How do you guys deal
emotionally with things?

01:40:32.690 --> 01:40:35.660
How do you reconcile your memories

01:40:35.760 --> 01:40:38.690
with the endless repetition of the present?

01:40:39.230 --> 01:40:42.200
I guess you become forgetful.

01:40:42.330 --> 01:40:46.700
Only your hazy dream-like state
keeps you sane.

01:40:46.840 --> 01:40:51.640
Yesterday, last month and last year
are indistinguishable.

01:40:51.740 --> 01:40:54.680
It's just one big blur. Am I right?

01:40:54.780 --> 01:40:57.910
That's how it is for me anyway.

01:40:58.050 --> 01:41:00.910
Ever since I was little, it's been this way.

01:41:01.050 --> 01:41:04.420
It was like I was in a daze and half asleep.

01:41:04.550 --> 01:41:05.850
That's what people said.

01:41:05.950 --> 01:41:08.080
Can't you see it yourself?

01:41:09.790 --> 01:41:13.850
Did you know that Kildren
used to be a Rostock's patent?

01:41:13.960 --> 01:41:18.490
You were the accidental by-product
of researches on gene modulators.

01:41:18.600 --> 01:41:23.230
The name intended for the new drug
was used for you guys instead.

01:41:23.370 --> 01:41:25.400
So you're not one of us?

01:41:25.540 --> 01:41:29.710
You Kildren don't age.
You go on living forever.

01:41:29.810 --> 01:41:33.840
Nobody knew at first.
When they found out, nobody believed it.

01:41:33.950 --> 01:41:36.510
But then the rumors started.

01:41:36.620 --> 01:41:39.610
"There are people who don't die
unless killed in battle!"

01:41:41.320 --> 01:41:45.190
I just don't know. Am I a Kildren, too?

01:41:45.290 --> 01:41:50.430
Where did I hear about this?
Did I read it somewhere? Is it true?

01:41:50.570 --> 01:41:54.400
It's all just a bunch of vague impressions.

01:41:54.500 --> 01:41:57.700
Am I talking from actual experience or not?

01:41:57.810 --> 01:41:59.970
There's nothing to grab hold of.

01:42:01.310 --> 01:42:06.610
I guess it's unlikely
that I'm the only one who's not a Kildren.

01:42:06.750 --> 01:42:11.710
How long have I been flying
and killing people?

01:42:11.820 --> 01:42:17.160
Every night, I wonder where,
when and how I ended up like this.

01:42:18.590 --> 01:42:22.660
But I can't remember. I can't remember!

01:42:22.800 --> 01:42:24.600
I try so hard...

01:42:24.700 --> 01:42:29.470
But I can only remember the same
few memories of my childhood.

01:42:43.950 --> 01:42:47.010
It looked like you enjoy playing with kids.

01:42:48.960 --> 01:42:52.020
At my old base,
I got to know some of the volunteers.

01:42:52.160 --> 01:42:55.460
I just helped find party venues, that's all.

01:42:56.470 --> 01:42:58.300
I love to watch kids.

01:42:58.400 --> 01:43:01.630
I imagine the childhood I might have had.

01:43:01.740 --> 01:43:06.470
I mean, it's possible that
I was born at the age I am now.

01:43:06.580 --> 01:43:11.880
The thought that maybe I didn't grow up
sort of knocks me off my feet.

01:43:12.010 --> 01:43:16.040
How about you?
Doesn't it make you feel uncertain?

01:43:17.690 --> 01:43:21.250
I think Kusanagi shot that guy, Jinroh,

01:43:21.390 --> 01:43:25.160
for his sake, so that he could just end it all.

01:43:27.060 --> 01:43:31.020
- But he didn't die.
- He didn't?

01:43:31.130 --> 01:43:33.100
No, he turned into you.

01:43:33.240 --> 01:43:35.930
He was brought back as a different person,

01:43:36.070 --> 01:43:39.370
with new memories implanted
and you're the result.

01:43:39.980 --> 01:43:42.210
You're the reincarnation of Jinroh.

01:43:42.310 --> 01:43:47.180
Otherwise, the skill set he had
as a pilot would have been lost,

01:43:47.280 --> 01:43:49.940
as well as his capabilities as a weapon.

01:43:50.920 --> 01:43:53.750
Why doesn't anyone notice?

01:43:53.890 --> 01:43:56.260
They just pretend that they don't

01:43:56.390 --> 01:44:00.230
until you figure it out for yourself.

01:44:00.330 --> 01:44:04.100
That's an interesting view.
How is the coffee?

01:44:07.240 --> 01:44:10.100
It was delicious. Thank you.

01:44:10.240 --> 01:44:14.440
It was an interesting discussion for me, too.
Thank you.

01:44:47.810 --> 01:44:49.780
Why are you doing this?

01:44:52.780 --> 01:44:54.940
You'd better put that away.

01:44:56.720 --> 01:45:01.950
- Or hand the gun over here to me.
- This is my gun.

01:45:03.490 --> 01:45:06.480
- Let me borrow it, then.
- What for?

01:45:08.500 --> 01:45:12.020
I'll do it for you. I'll shoot Kusanagi.

01:45:13.900 --> 01:45:15.700
That's a fine idea.

01:45:44.930 --> 01:45:47.490
Leave the room now, Mitsuya.

01:45:50.170 --> 01:45:52.400
If you want to die, go ahead!

01:46:12.030 --> 01:46:14.090
Mind if I smoke?

01:46:15.100 --> 01:46:18.090
Feel free. It's your office.

01:46:20.940 --> 01:46:22.960
You killed Jinroh Kurita?

01:46:23.670 --> 01:46:24.930
Yes.

01:46:28.080 --> 01:46:29.570
He asked you to?

01:46:29.680 --> 01:46:30.980
Yes.

01:46:31.810 --> 01:46:33.470
Did you love him?

01:46:36.120 --> 01:46:37.210
Yes.

01:46:38.950 --> 01:46:40.580
Kannami.

01:46:43.020 --> 01:46:45.420
I want you to shoot me with that gun.

01:46:45.530 --> 01:46:47.120
You want me to kill you?

01:46:47.260 --> 01:46:51.600
Yes. This time, it's your turn to kill me.

01:46:53.000 --> 01:46:54.300
Please.

01:47:12.020 --> 01:47:13.490
You have to live.

01:47:13.620 --> 01:47:15.820
Until you can find a way to change things.

01:50:11.230 --> 01:50:15.730
You can change the side of the road
that you walk down every day.

01:50:17.210 --> 01:50:21.370
Even if the road is the same,
you can still see new things.

01:50:23.010 --> 01:50:25.310
Isn't that enough to live for?

01:50:26.920 --> 01:50:31.080
Or does that mean that it isn't enough?

01:50:38.260 --> 01:50:42.860
Warning, enemy in sight!
Two o'clock, same height!

01:50:42.960 --> 01:50:44.400
It's a J-2!

01:50:44.530 --> 01:50:46.160
Everyone retreat!

01:50:48.900 --> 01:50:51.740
Cairn, where are you going? Get back!

01:50:52.370 --> 01:50:57.570
- I'm gonna cover you!
- Quit it! This is my game.

01:51:02.280 --> 01:51:07.190
Even if the road is the same
you can see different things.

01:51:08.120 --> 01:51:11.090
Isn't that enough to live for?

01:51:14.260 --> 01:51:15.890
I'll kill my father.

02:00:39.160 --> 02:00:40.320
Enter.

02:00:49.200 --> 02:00:52.470
Isamu Hiiragi, I've been assigned here.

02:00:56.710 --> 02:00:58.770
I'm Suito Kusanagi.

02:00:58.880 --> 02:01:00.970
I've been waiting for you.
